    "body": "This draft continues the full Rev1.18 candidate rebuild from existing source and the frozen plan. Formal unit, backend, production and device acceptance remain open.\n\nCurrent published source: `d53eea63539d5829ff0ac4f5aa7b55155a3c7491`.\n\n### Latest behavior\n\nAn actual MT5 EA PLACED acknowledgment previously became UNKNOWN in the pull adapter and lost its native order ID. It now remains ACCEPTED with the exact unsigned 64-bit ticket, zero filled quantity, no invented average fill or position, and protection confirmed only by the original explicit boolean. Contradictory acknowledgments require original reconciliation. Missing native time remains unknown.\n\nSubmit independently reads the first durable SQL claim/result. Reopen, stale current availability and expired-command replay preserve the original valid completion and receipt hash without another claim. Missing/corrupt completion clocks retain known native effects with unavailable local completion time. Existing supported entry types remain MARKET.\n\n### Verification\n\n- **5,272 passed, zero failures/errors/skips**, across full trading and selected original gateway SQL/HTTP/private-core/schema/scope checks. Actual SQLite/PostgreSQL; zero Python storage-audit violations. Every call ran once. All **1,259 pinned inputs plus two legacy fixtures** independently match committed Git objects. Owned PostgreSQL independently confirmed removed.\n- Actual EA function bodies run through the explicit C++ terminal API model; signed HTTP/SQL polling and recovery execute in the source suite. **2,880 original test functions retain identical AST**. Eight additional real-SQL checks preserve original terminal/uncertain claims after explicit command expiry.\n- Baseline reproduced two ACCEPTED-to-UNKNOWN failures. First affected rerun retained 105 passes/one fixture failure: recovery fixture omitted the original registered account binding. Binding was restored in the fixture; production identity matching remains strict. Final focused 161 checks overlap the broad run.\n- Genuine hook, required-baseline committed ledger **GREEN192**, normal push and independent exact remote readback: succeeded. Canonical manifest: **10,358 files, zero mismatches**. Owner/frontend and frozen scope guards pass. Mutation consistency preserves 374 identities/383 edits; it is not local mutation execution.\n- Fresh [exact-head main40700452416](https://github.com/Vanguduza/Van/actions/runs/40700452416) and four supporting workflows have started; no results claimed yet.\n- Parent373 main40692934675 finished **FAILURE**: all 17 public jobs succeeded; mandatory failures are the unprovisioned DDS read key and ledger checker absent from trusted main. Four supporting workflows succeeded. Original hosted logs report 4,987 trading passes/one declared private-DDS skip, 26 PostgreSQL passes and 117 voice passes. The selected JUnit archive download returned JSON metadata under a ZIP declaration and was rejected; no archive verification claimed.\n- Production EA bytes are unchanged from parent373, whose original official MetaEditor artifact was independently verified: valid signatures, exact source/blob, fresh binary, zero errors/warnings, invalid probe four errors/no binary. This establishes SOURCE_COMPILED, without connected-account/provider/financial/device qualification.\n\n### Full scope and continuation\n\n[Execution method](docs/rebuild/rev118/BUILD_EXECUTION_PLAN.md), [workmap](docs/rebuild/rev118/SOURCE_WORKMAP.json) and [pending-receipt evidence](docs/rebuild/rev118/receipts/MT5_PENDING_RECEIPTS_SOURCE_20261028.json) retain all **131 units, 324 requirements, 1,610 acceptance identities, 234 contexts, 349 actions and 93 planned features**. Original frontend coverage remains 42 groups/105 functions/78 surfaces.\n\nComplete shared all-origin transactional cash/margin/stop-risk reservations, post-entry margin floors, fee/fill contingencies, qualified FX/contract migration, active-policy arbitration, working-order/partial-fill/cancel reconciliation and native economic finality. ACCEPTED is never a fill, settlement or reservation release. All payment/manual/handover, feeds/depth/entitlements, forecast/learning/crypto, assistant and security/operations functions remain required. Profitability is evaluated with evidence, never guaranteed.\n\nAndroid must use its provisioned production profile on Van trading core without owner-entered backend addresses. Frontend redesign stays behind BG-001. Independent admission, signing, deployment and actual Artemis/Samsung S24 Ultra acceptance remain open. Frozen package bytes, authorization records, hooks and ledger integrity are preserved.\n",
